WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:32.833
<b>In the previous several verses, </b>
<b>Lord Krishna described</b>

2
00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:39.958
<b>various types of sacrifices and renunciations, </b>
<b>and explained their results.</b>

3
00:00:39.958 --> 00:00:45.583
<b>And now he is telling about the </b>
<b>basis of all these sacrifices.</b>

4
00:00:50.375 --> 00:00:51.916
<b>Lord Krishna says</b>

5
00:00:51.916 --> 00:00:55.916
<b>that the detailed description of all these </b>
<b>various sacrifices is in the Vedas.</b>

6
00:00:55.916 --> 00:00:59.750
<b>And these sacrifices arise from different actions,</b>

7
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.541
<b>and one who gains knowledge of them, </b>
<b>who follows them,</b>

8
00:01:03.541 --> 00:01:06.791
<b>will be freed from material bondage.</b>

9
00:01:06.791 --> 00:01:11.791
<b>Here we find two common foundations </b>
<b>for all these sacrifices.</b>

10
00:01:11.791 --> 00:01:12.958
<b>The first foundation -</b>

11
00:01:12.958 --> 00:01:16.125
<b>the description of all these </b>
<b>sacrifices is in the Vedas.</b>

12
00:01:16.125 --> 00:01:17.791
<b>And the second foundation is that</b>

13
00:01:17.791 --> 00:01:21.416
<b>all these sacrifices have the </b>
<b>same primary objective,</b>

14
00:01:21.416 --> 00:01:25.333
<b>to attain liberation through actions.</b>

15
00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:30.000
<b>If you have paid attention, then all these </b>
<b>sacrifices involved action,</b>

16
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.250
<b>somewhere physical action, </b>
<b>somewhere mental action.</b>

17
00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:34.375
<b>Somewhere labor,</b>

18
00:01:34.375 --> 00:01:35.708
<b>somewhere study,</b>

19
00:01:35.708 --> 00:01:37.416
<b>and somewhere contemplation.</b>

20
00:01:37.416 --> 00:01:40.750
<b>In all these sacrifices, the renunciation</b>
<b>may be different,</b>

21
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.833
<b>the action may be different,</b>

22
00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:45.041
<b>the method may be different,</b>

23
00:01:45.041 --> 00:01:48.416
<b>but the purpose of all is the same.</b>

24
00:01:48.416 --> 00:01:53.000
<b>To elevate man above this materiality </b>
<b>and grant him liberation.</b>

25
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:59.666
<b>Through these sacrificial actions, man is purified </b>
<b>of all sins and is ultimately liberated.</b>

26
00:01:59.666 --> 00:02:06.333
<b>Here a very deep point is also being made,</b>
<b>which is extremely important to understand.</b>

27
00:02:06.333 --> 00:02:09.958
<b>That inactivity is never appropriate.</b>

28
00:02:09.958 --> 00:02:12.208
<b>The path of action is the right one,</b>

29
00:02:12.208 --> 00:02:16.416
<b>and this very path will lead to spiritual progress.</b>

30
00:02:16.416 --> 00:02:18.666
<b>Many times a person thinks</b>

31
00:02:18.666 --> 00:02:21.541
<b>that to attain liberation, </b>
<b>the meaning of renunciation</b>

32
00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:25.958
<b> is to give up one's duties </b>
<b>and run away from action.</b>

33
00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:32.041
<b>But the truth is that the means to attain </b>
<b>liberation is to understand one's duties,</b>

34
00:02:32.041 --> 00:02:35.291
<b>to perform one's actions selflessly,</b>

35
00:02:35.291 --> 00:02:38.708
<b>and to bring the spirit of sacrifice into them.</b>

36
00:02:38.708 --> 00:02:41.250
<b>This knowledge is being given to Arjuna,</b>

37
00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.833
<b>but it is applicable to all of us.</b>

38
00:02:43.833 --> 00:02:47.125
<b>Selflessness will have to be </b>
<b>chosen instead of selfishness.</b>

39
00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:50.416
<b>Renunciation will have to be </b>
<b>chosen instead of enjoyment.</b>

40
00:02:50.416 --> 00:02:54.000
<b>Action will have to be chosen instead of inactivity.</b>

41
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.500
<b>Actions will have to be performed,</b>

42
00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.041
<b>but the sentiment behind them </b>
<b>will have to be changed.</b>

43
00:02:59.041 --> 00:03:05.041
<b>And this will lead man to spiritual </b>
<b>purification and liberation.</b>

44
00:03:09.791 --> 00:03:11.791
<b>Sacrifice –</b>

45
00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:16.458
<b>in simple terms it can be divided into two parts,</b>

46
00:03:16.458 --> 00:03:18.208
<b>the first part –</b>

47
00:03:18.208 --> 00:03:21.083
<b>dedicating something of one's own,</b>

48
00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:23.000
<b>and the second part -</b>

49
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.708
<b>not having any expectation in return.</b>

50
00:03:26.708 --> 00:03:30.208
<b>And sacrificing while performing actions,</b>

51
00:03:30.208 --> 00:03:33.750
<b>this is the essence of this verse.</b>

52
00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:38.041
<b>Humans can apply this in any area of his life.</b>

53
00:03:38.041 --> 00:03:42.291
<b>All of you have special talents and abilities</b>

54
00:03:42.291 --> 00:03:46.625
<b>through which you contribute to society.</b>

55
00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:54.375
<b>Just keep in mind that you do it with a</b>
<b>spirit of service or benevolence to others.</b>

56
00:03:54.375 --> 00:04:00.041
<b>And when you keep the spirit of service </b>
<b>in your mind instead of personal gain,</b>

57
00:04:00.041 --> 00:04:03.916
<b>then that very action will become a sacrifice.</b>

58
00:04:03.916 --> 00:04:09.791
<b>If you are in the field of medicine, then </b>
<b>along with treating patients,</b>

59
00:04:09.791 --> 00:04:14.833
<b>you also boost their morale, </b>
<b>give them positive thinking.</b>

60
00:04:14.833 --> 00:04:17.833
<b>This too is selfless.</b>

61
00:04:17.833 --> 00:04:19.416
<b>Now think,</b>

62
00:04:19.416 --> 00:04:23.291
<b>in your personal life, there are </b>
<b>immense opportunities</b>

63
00:04:23.291 --> 00:04:27.166
<b>that can lead you to spiritual progress.</b>

64
00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:31.250
<b>This will also bring a flow of contentment in life.</b>

65
00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:40.166
<b>Different types of sacrifices were talked about,</b>

66
00:04:40.166 --> 00:04:44.208
<b>sacrifice and action were talked about.</b>

67
00:04:44.208 --> 00:04:49.291
<b>If we just deepen our perspective,</b>

68
00:04:49.291 --> 00:04:55.708
<b>we will know that this is all </b>
<b>directly visible in the family.</b>

69
00:04:55.708 --> 00:04:58.916
<b>Because in a family there are different people,</b>

70
00:04:58.916 --> 00:05:01.333
<b>everyone has their own interests,</b>

71
00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:04.416
<b>their own actions, there is mutual love,</b>

72
00:05:04.416 --> 00:05:10.291
<b>and due to this love there are also </b>
<b>many kinds of selfless sacrifices.</b>

73
00:05:10.291 --> 00:05:14.166
<b>Take the example of a married couple,</b>

74
00:05:14.166 --> 00:05:22.041
<b>where one person, by sacrificing his time, </b>
<b>brings economic stability for the family,</b>

75
00:05:22.041 --> 00:05:30.041
<b>while the other spends his time in nurturing</b>
<b>the children, contributes to their education.</b>

76
00:05:30.041 --> 00:05:32.208
<b>Here there is duty,</b>

77
00:05:32.208 --> 00:05:34.041
<b>there is love,</b>

78
00:05:34.041 --> 00:05:35.666
<b>there is action,</b>

79
00:05:35.666 --> 00:05:37.041
<b>there is sacrifice,</b>

80
00:05:37.041 --> 00:05:42.208
<b>just no personal selfishness.</b>

81
00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:44.500
<b>This is indeed a sacrifice.</b>

82
00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.541
<b>And for this reason,</b>

83
00:05:46.541 --> 00:05:51.875
<b>these two pillars of the family should </b>
<b>be viewed with equal vision. </b>

84
00:05:51.875 --> 00:05:54.958
<b>Both should be equally respected.</b>

85
00:05:54.958 --> 00:05:57.791
<b>Both are worthy of appreciation.</b>

86
00:05:57.791 --> 00:05:59.125
<b>Consider this,</b>

87
00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:06.000
<b>where else will you find a better example </b>
<b>of selfless sacrifice than family.</b>

88
00:06:10.541 --> 00:06:17.916
<b>Having the spirit of sacrifice at the workplace </b>
<b>not only improves your personal thinking,</b>

89
00:06:17.916 --> 00:06:18.916
<b>but</b>

90
00:06:18.916 --> 00:06:22.000
<b>also improves the environment </b>
<b>of the entire organization.</b>

91
00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:28.000
<b>The only requirement is to change </b>
<b>one's perspective a little bit.</b>

92
00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.666
<b>No work should be considered small.</b>

93
00:06:30.666 --> 00:06:31.875
<b>And along with that,</b>

94
00:06:31.875 --> 00:06:37.541
<b>everyone should strive to contribute more </b>
<b>than the organization's expectations.</b>

95
00:06:37.541 --> 00:06:39.166
<b>For example,</b>

96
00:06:39.166 --> 00:06:43.666
<b>a senior official appointed </b>
<b>to a leadership position.</b>

97
00:06:43.666 --> 00:06:47.416
<b>Who takes out a few moments</b>
<b>from his personal time</b>

98
00:06:47.416 --> 00:06:51.708
<b>and provides training to others just to help them.</b>

99
00:06:51.708 --> 00:06:57.916
<b>While someone else contributes more than </b>
<b>the expected work for customer service.</b>

100
00:06:57.916 --> 00:07:04.291
<b>These are all sacrifices or offerings, </b>
<b>and are worthy of appreciation.</b>

101
00:07:04.291 --> 00:07:10.666
<b>It is important for the organization, </b>
<b>and especially for senior officials,</b>

102
00:07:10.666 --> 00:07:14.083
<b>to encourage all such contributions.</b>

103
00:07:14.083 --> 00:07:17.041
<b>This will bring many positive changes.</b>

104
00:07:17.041 --> 00:07:20.333
<b>Think how positive the environment will be,</b>

105
00:07:20.333 --> 00:07:27.083
<b>where the organization selflessly appreciates </b>
<b>the good work of the employees,</b>

106
00:07:27.083 --> 00:07:32.000
<b>and people give selfless contributions</b>
<b>beyond expectations.</b>

